course: dictionary
lesson: 8994
title: One word, three meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word size has more than one meaning, so you need the context to choose the right one. Look at the words around it. «The jaguar has the strongest bite for its size of any big cat» is about how big the jaguar is.
explain: Shoes and clothes use size as a set measure. If your shoe size is 3, that is a number on a scale, not how big your foot looks. «Money comes in all sizes too» means money is made in different amounts or shapes, so size means how big or small each coin or note is.
explain: Size can also mean how many. In maths, «multiply the number of groups by the size of one group» means how many things are in one group. Ask yourself: is the word talking about a measure, a count, or how big something is? Then swap your meaning into the sentence to check it.
fact: Size can mean how big or small something is.
fact: A size can be one of the set measures for clothes and shoes, such as shoe size 3.
fact: Size can mean how many things there are in a group.
fact: In maths, the size of one group is one factor when you multiply, and it is the answer when you divide a total by the number of groups.
exercise: «The jaguar has the strongest bite for its size of any big cat.» What does size mean here? | Judging how big someone is | How many jaguars are in a group | A set measure for shoes | *How big the jaguar is
exercise: Mia says her shoe size is 3. What does size mean? | How big her feet look | *A set measure for shoes | How many shoes she owns | Judging how big her feet are
exercise: «Multiply the number of groups by the size of one group.» What does size mean? | How big one group is on a map | How big a number is | *How many things are in one group | A set measure for clothes
test: Jade's teacher says each team has a size of six. What does size mean? | Judging how tall the team is | How big the team's bodies are | A set measure for shoes | *How many people are in the team
test: «One size fits all» means what? | Only one shoe will fit | Everything is too big | *One thing works for everyone | Everyone is the same height
exam: «Money comes in all sizes too.» Which meaning of size is used? | Judging how big someone is | *How big or small something is | How many are in one group | A set measure for shoes and clothes
